# Packaging-exclusion patterns, read by scripts/security_scan.py's --package
# mode (row 37, prior art: tripleyak/SkillForge). One pattern per line;
# trailing "/" excludes a directory (and everything under it) at any depth;
# no "/" matches by filename/dirname at any depth; a pattern containing "/"
# elsewhere is matched against the relative path.
#
# This file lives at the plugin root per the architecture tree, and doubles
# as the reference example for the convention: scripts/security_scan.py
# reads .skillignore from inside whatever directory is being scanned/
# packaged, so an authored skill's own exclusions belong in
# <that-skill>/.skillignore, not here. creating-skills/ itself doesn't need
# one — the row 34 discipline this file documents is exactly why: no
# README.md/CHANGELOG.md/install guide ever lands inside the skill
# subdirectory in the first place, so there's nothing there to exclude.

README.md
LICENSE
CHANGELOG.md
CONTEXT.md
docs/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
